bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    smf_native_codegen_data_rel_ro_subsection_2026_11_09, 0, "2026-11-09 phase-2 gate lane (work/boot-t2-testrunner-20261109): MC/DC-off waiver -> real SMF path -> child SIGBUS with .data.rel.ro.subsection codegen error (aarch64 host). Sequenced behind the run_one_direct flag-drop fix and the _ElfWriter/writer startup-spin P1."
    smf_native_codegen_data_rel_ro_subsection_2026_11_09, 1, "2026-11-10 fix lane (work/p2-smf-data-rel-ro): root cause located, not in 70.backend. The quoted error is the Rust seed: execution.rs:145 (Failed to preserve SMF imports/relocations from object code) wrapping object_parser.rs:304 (relocation source section <name> is not executable code) -- the seed SMF v1.0 reloc record has no source-section field, so an LLVM .data.rel.ro.<sym> pointer table (SHF_ALLOC|SHF_WRITE PROGBITS with R_AARCH64_ABS64/R_X86_64_64 relocs) cannot be represented and the seed fails closed. The pure-Simple twin was WORSE (fail-open): --mode=smf packaging (driver_aot_smf_output.spl via build_smf_with_relocations / generate_smf_with_options) extracts .text* and .rela.text* only, silently dropping the relocated data section -> code dereferences an unrelocated table -> child SIGBUS. Fix: smf_elf_parser.spl elf_relocated_non_code_section() names the first SHF_ALLOC non-exec section targeted by a SHT_RELA/SHT_REL (sh_info), skipping .eh_frame*/.note*; driver_aot_smf_output.spl now returns CodegenError naming it instead of emitting a broken SMF. Specs: test/01_unit/compiler/driver/smf_elf_relocated_data_section_spec.spl (red 0/9 -> green 9/9; .data.rel.ro.<sym>, .data.rel.ro, .rodata.<sym>, .data.<sym>, .init_array named; code-only, .eh_frame, non-alloc, non-ELF -> empty) and prevention test/01_unit/compiler/driver/smf_group_object_section_naming_spec.spl (5/5: the v1.2 group-object path keeps .data.rel.ro.<sym> as a named R|W Data section, records it as the relocation source, and classifies .text/.rodata.<sym>/.data.<sym> through the same builder). Not fixed here: the seed-side representation (needs a source-section field in the seed SmfRelocation + loader support, cargo build) -- the real --mode=smf representational fix is to route relocated-data objects through the v1.2 group adapter (smf_group_object_adapter.spl), which is x86_64-only today. Collateral: SMF section-table names are a 16-byte inline field, so .data.rel.ro.local and longer subsection names are truncated silently (cosmetic, loader keys on type)."

